{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1452487-hedgespinning-questions","id":1452487,"title":"Hedgespinning Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-16T09:06:49-07:00","id":1452487,"title":"Hedgespinning Questions","content":"Hello everyone, <br /> <br /> I have a potentially stupid question here. Suppose two changelings are battling each other via Hedgespinning. For some reason, I\u2019m unclear how one defends against certain Hedgespinning shifts. For instance, using a Subtle Shift to introduce a personal Tilt on your opponent, or decreasing your opponent\u2019s Speed. Is there a roll to defend against this, or does it simply take effect if the attacker rolls enough successes?<br /> <br /> Normally when a Condition or Tilt is inflicted due to a supernatural effect, the effect gets to be Resisted or Contested. But I don\u2019t see anything like that for Hedgespinning. <br /> <br /> The closest thing that I\u2019ve seen is under Paradigm Shifts. There is the option of paying five successes to force a Clash of Wills to stop a Hedgespinning action. Is a Paradigm Shift the only way to defend against a targeted Hedgespinning effect, even a Subtle Shift? Am I missing something?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25750,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25750-holy-hell-thats-hot","user":"Holy-Hell-Thats-Hot","date":". 06-16-2021, 12:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25750-holy-hell-thats-hot","name":"Holy-Hell-Thats-Hot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T11:05:11-07:00","id":1452508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy-Hell-Thats-Hot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1452487-hedgespinning-questions#post1452487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello everyone,<br /> <br /> I have a potentially stupid question here. Suppose two changelings are battling each other via Hedgespinning. For some reason, I\u2019m unclear how one defends against certain Hedgespinning shifts. For instance, using a Subtle Shift to introduce a personal Tilt on your opponent, or decreasing your opponent\u2019s Speed. Is there a roll to defend against this, or does it simply take effect if the attacker rolls enough successes?</div> </div> </div> </div>It simply takes effect unless the target has an ability that would counteract the effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Normally when a Condition or Tilt is inflicted due to a supernatural effect, the effect gets to be Resisted or Contested. But I don\u2019t see anything like that for Hedgespinning. </div> </div> </div>Hedgespinning is weird, it's technically acting on the Hedge itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The closest thing that I\u2019ve seen is under Paradigm Shifts. There is the option of paying five successes to force a Clash of Wills to stop a Hedgespinning action. Is a Paradigm Shift the only way to defend against a targeted Hedgespinning effect, even a Subtle Shift? Am I missing something?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance. </div> </div> </div>Any supernatural power that would protect against the results of the Hedgespinning effect would also protect you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}